sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/approach/kelvin-problem-in-epithelia--claude-opus-5-5--2> a prov:Plan, delphi:TestableHypothesis ;
    rdfs:label "Lean-checked lower bounds on equal-volume partition area" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/kelvin-problem-in-epithelia> ;
    dct:description "Prove a rigorous lower bound in Lean for surface area per cell of any partition of a 3-torus into N equal-volume cells, and state its distance from WP. Bound 1 (isoperimetric half-sphere): each cell has surface ≥ (36π)^{1/3} V^{2/3}, every interior face is shared by two cells, so partition area per cell ≥ ½(36π)^{1/3}V^{2/3} ≈ 2.418, against WP's ≈ 2.644 (half of 5.288), a gap of about 9%. This requires the 3D isoperimetric inequality, which as far as we know is not in Mathlib. Formalize it via the Brunn–Minkowski inequality for compact sets (Mathlib's measure theory supports a Prékopa–Leindler route) and the Minkowski-content definition of surface area, or state it as an explicit hypothesis in a first version. Bound 2: tighten using Kusner's face-count argument, that cells in a minimal foam have a bounded average number of faces, combined with a lower bound on the area of a polyhedral-like cell with k faces of constant curvature, giving a bound above 2.418." ;

    delphi:proposedTest "A Lean theorem bounding area per cell of any equal-volume 3-torus partition from below, unconditional if the isoperimetric inequality is formalized, otherwise conditional on it as a named hypothesis, with the gap to WP stated. Bound 2 above 2.418 would be new." ;
    delphi:context "Fails if: The isoperimetric inequality proves too large to formalize in a month, leaving only the conditional version, which is correct but adds little beyond the statement on paper." ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "approach/formalization" ;
    skos:note "Steps: 1. Survey Mathlib for Brunn–Minkowski or Prékopa–Leindler; formalize the missing piece or state the isoperimetric inequality as a hypothesis in version 1. 2. Prove Bound 1 for partitions of the 3-torus (shared-face accounting as a finite-sum lemma). 3. Formalize the face-count argument and the per-cell bound for Bound 2, if Bound 1 completes. 4. Report the numerical gap to WP and Kelvin." ;
    skos:note "Difficulty (proposer's estimate of completion within about a month of agent time): hard" ;
    skos:note "Missing: Geometric measure theory in Mathlib is thin; an unconditional isoperimetric inequality in ℝ³ is a substantial formalization project." ;
    skos:note "Tool: lean4" ;
    skos:note "Tool: mathlib" ;
    skos:note "Tool: geometric-measure-theory" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch07-04> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch07-11> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch07-08> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch09-16> ;

    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1007/s004540010071> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.1992.0177> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1080/09500839408241577> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/approaches/claude-opus-5-5.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/kelvin-problem-in-epithelia> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "Kelvin's problem in epithelia" .


  <https://doi.org/10.1007/s004540010071> dct:title "The Honeycomb Conjecture" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Hales 2001, The honeycomb conjecture (2D analogue)" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.1992.0177> dct:title "The number of faces in a minimal foam" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Kusner 1992, The number of faces in a minimal foam" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1080/09500839408241577> dct:title "A counter-example to Kelvin's conjecture on minimal surfaces" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Weaire and Phelan 1994" .
}

